WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.968
- The only thing Americans
love more than cars

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:05.317
is modifying their cars in
completely illegal ways.

00:00:05.317 --> 00:00:06.740
Now, this is America.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.423
So, let's start with guns.

00:00:08.423 --> 00:00:10.850
Now this is a Polish military vehicle,

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.720
but plenty of Americans
see this and think,

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.690
yeah, that's exactly the car I need

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:15.973
to head over to Walmart.

00:00:15.973 --> 00:00:19.620
No, honestly, I think this
is probably what F1 needs

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.870
in the next season.

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.700
But there are times when having a gun

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.420
mounted inside or outside of
a vehicle might come in handy.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:26.910
Like when you're Nick Fury

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.640
and you need to evade a SWAT team,

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:30.945
or if you're James Bond.

00:00:30.945 --> 00:00:33.820
(guns shooting)

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.070
Or when you're trying
to get around the idiots

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:37.900
in the DC trucker convoy.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.860
Now, obviously it's
pretty much indisputable

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.090
that this looks really cool,

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.150
but it's obviously illegal
to mount a gun to your car.

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.350
It's not like you can go on Amazon

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.374
and buy a rack that lets you
put a gun on your actual car.

00:00:48.374 --> 00:00:52.100
Well, there are actually
lots of different gun mounts

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.670
for sale on Amazon that
you can put on your car

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:57.360
like this Vulcan quick
draw magnetic high grip

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.390
handgun mount holster,

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.460
which clamps to your car, your desk, wall,

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:03.440
basically anywhere you
think you might want

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:04.990
to quick draw a handgun from.

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:08.990
And here's a magnetic car
gun mount for just 29.99.

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:10.510
Now are any of these products legal?

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:12.200
Well, some of them are.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.730
It's generally legal to install something

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:15.010
that lets you mount a weapon

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.010
to your vehicle or other surface.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.520
But once you've actually
installed loaded weapon

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.910
it's more likely to be completely illegal.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:22.980
So let me break this down.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.470
First of all, in some
states you need a license

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:25.640
to carry a concealed weapon.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:27.720
So in those states, driving
with a concealed weapon

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.520
would be illegal unless you are licensed.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.834
Now what about mounting
a long gun to the car?

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:34.854
Not surprisingly, not legal.

00:01:34.854 --> 00:01:37.840
In Pennsylvania for example,
no person, even a holder

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.640
of a license to carry a firearm
may carry a loaded long gun

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:42.473
in a vehicle

00:01:42.473 --> 00:01:43.470
and you also can't get around the law

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.710
by switching to an ATV
or snowmobile either

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.600
since it's generally unlawful to operate

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.770
or ride any snowmobile
or ATV in possession

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:50.880
of a loaded firearm.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.810
Now what about non-working
firearms for show?

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:55.680
Now in some states you
might be able to get away

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.420
with displaying a dummy
firearm in a vehicle.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.940
This is common for world war II reenacters

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:03.011
who use decommissioned
military transport vehicles

00:02:03.011 --> 00:02:04.870
and weapons from that era.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.410
However, you should not assume

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:07.778
that inoperable weapons are legal.

00:02:07.778 --> 00:02:10.550
Brandishing an imitation or dummy firearm

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.090
is a crime in California.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.440
But then what about the
old private land loophole?

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:15.390
Now it might be possible

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:17.590
for you to mount a 50
caliber machine gun on a Jeep

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:19.426
if you have the money and
fire it on private land

00:02:19.426 --> 00:02:21.330
in a state with few gun laws.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:23.140
But if you drive around
the neighborhood with it

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.890
even in a gun friendly state,
you risk being arrested

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:28.210
for a whole multitude of different laws

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:30.420
violating brandishing
laws, disturbing the peace,

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.480
perceived threatening of other people.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.120
And you know, driving
around in a weapon of war

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.620
generally framed upon by
many different jurisdictions.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:43.140
Even if you're James Bond.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.150
But maybe guns per se aren't your thing.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.801
What if you wanted to turn
your car into a flame thrower?

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:50.140
(dramatic music)

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.890
Well, a lot of people
surprisingly had this idea.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.540
In the 1990s, a South African
invented a flame thrower

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:57.820
called a blaster

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.630
that was mounted to the
car's undercarriage.

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:01.460
The blaster was meant to deter carjackings

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:03.490
by burning anyone who attempted it.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.860
And as you can see it
definitely had the capability

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:07.120
of barbecuing a human.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.200
Now it did not go over particularly well.

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.860
And the cost of the
modification was so high

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.890
that only a few hundred were sold.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:15.804
Still that's a few hundred of modification

00:03:15.804 --> 00:03:18.520
that could turn your car
into a human barbecuer.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:20.800
But what about in the good old US of A?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.560
Can you put a flame thrower

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.440
on the undercarriage of your car?

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:27.610
Well, basically no, because as
I explained in a recent video

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:29.480
flame throwers are totally legal

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.830
and you have the right to
own one as an American.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.810
You can have a flame thrower
on your private property

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.670
but modifications to a car
or a truck are different.

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:38.670
So let's look at the kits
that modify your exhaust

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:39.720
to shoot flames.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.020
Amazon sells them.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.630
You can buy older ones on eBay.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:43.960
Not that you should.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.360
If you did the hot licks exhaust kits

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.230
have a lifetime warranty.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.630
So is this legal?

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:50.730
Absolutely not.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.810
If you try this in Virginia,
the state can throw you in jail

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.610
and suspend your driver's
license for six months.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:57.210
A lot of states including
Virginia have specific laws

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:59.760
that prohibit devices for the
emission of smoke screens,

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.860
gas projectors or flame throwers,

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.560
which are prohibited in that state.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.430
That means that if you do
anything to modify your muffler

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.120
so that smoke or flame shoot out

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:08.500
you could be charged with a felony.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:09.910
And once you start meddling with systems

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:11.890
that control emissions that runs a foul

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.540
of environmental regulations.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:16.100
Now, if you've ever been to
a tractor pull competition

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.380
you've probably witnessed coal rolling.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:20.830
Now at these competitions
modified trucks and tractors

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:23.310
drag a metal sled filled with
a weight across the course.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.930
And the point is to determine
which vehicle is capable

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:28.050
of dragging the heaviest weight
over the longest distance.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.590
But see all that smoke.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:32.430
Some people have started
what's called rolling coal

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:33.570
on their own vehicles.

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:35.160
Some guys with diesel pickup trucks

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:37.220
have modified their trucks
to blow coal at people

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:38.506
who drive electric cars.

00:04:38.506 --> 00:04:41.180
And this modification allows
the driver to flip a switch

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:45.140
that spews a billow of dirty
coal smoke out of the exhaust.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.090
There are videos of this all over YouTube

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:48.820
of truckers rolling coal in the faces

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:50.760
of protestors, cyclists and runners

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.030
and the practices got more attention

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:54.110
when Texas teens flooded a
restaurant with coal smoke.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:57.620
The video became a hit on
TikTok and now many states

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.120
make this explicitly illegal

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:02.220
though it was probably already illegal

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.450
under general laws of applicability.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:06.910
Maryland outright banned it in 2017.

00:05:06.910 --> 00:05:08.900
And in the states that don't
specifically prohibit it.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:10.640
It's probably still illegal.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:11.473
You can get in big trouble

00:05:11.473 --> 00:05:12.570
because shooting a plume

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:15.360
of coal smoke is number
one, inherently dangerous

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:17.220
and is tied to other crimes.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:19.280
For example, a 16 year old Texas boy

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:21.060
driving a diesel pickup
thought it would be funny

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:22.770
to blow coal at eight cyclists.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.750
When he got close to
them, he hit six of them

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:25.700
with his truck.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:27.960
He was charged with six counts
of felony aggravated assault

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:28.793
with a deadly weapon.

00:05:28.793 --> 00:05:30.781
And rolling coal requires
a driver to have overridden

00:05:30.781 --> 00:05:33.300
or tampered with the
vehicle's emission controls

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.560
and tampering with those
emission control systems

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.550
is blatantly illegal
under the clean air act.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:41.090
And additionally, intentionally
blowing a huge plume

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:44.570
of black smoke at other people
almost certainly qualifies

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:47.140
as assault and battery, maybe
a public nuisance as well.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.510
So just because there's not
a specific regulation on this

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:52.260
it's still probably incredibly illegal.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:53.093
And of course rolling coal

00:05:53.093 --> 00:05:55.750
