00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:09.930
All right so let's talk in
a little bit more detail

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:11.421
about those radar detectors and jammers

00:12:11.421 --> 00:12:14.810
because I've been fascinated
with these things for years.

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:16.490
If you have a lead foot and the habit

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:18.470
of getting speeding tickets
you might have considered

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:21.230
getting a radar detector
or scrambler or jammer.

00:12:21.230 --> 00:12:23.300
Now what are these devices
and how do they work?

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:24.730
Now a radar detector is a device

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:27.647
that detects a police radar
wave that the police use

00:12:27.647 --> 00:12:30.580
with radar guns to measure
the speed of passing vehicles.

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:32.760
Detectors are only
meant to warn the driver

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:34.700
that police are monitoring the area.

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:36.610
They don't actually
interfere with radar signals

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:39.600
and in the US, it's not
illegal to use a radar detector

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:41.780
unless you're in Virginia
or Washington DC.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.998
However, in all states it's
illegal to use a radar detector

00:12:43.998 --> 00:12:47.290
in a commercial vehicle
weighing over 10,000 pounds.

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:48.800
Now why would that be?

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:51.120
Well, the idea is it's extra dangerous

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:53.380
for a commercial vehicle to
go above the speed limit.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:55.620
Especially since they may
be hauling dangerous goods

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:58.360
like oil and gas or
thousands and thousands

00:12:58.360 --> 00:12:59.960
of pounds of products.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.470
And some states have regulations

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:03.450
about where a radar
detector can be mounted.

00:13:03.450 --> 00:13:05.560
In California for instance,
it has to be mounted

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:06.460
on the dashboard.

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:08.450
Now radar jammers on the
other hand have been around

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:10.820
for many years, but
they're usually illegal.

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:11.670
And here's how they work.

00:13:11.670 --> 00:13:13.300
There's a computer in police radar guns

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:14.430
that measures the differential

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:16.070
between the reflected radar waves

00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:17.810
to calculate a vehicle speed

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:20.550
and jammers transmit a
signal to overpower the data

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:22.780
sent from the car to
the police radar guns.

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:25.570
And the FCC regulates the
frequencies used in radar guns

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.300
stating quote, "No person
shall willfully or maliciously

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:30.320
interfere with or cause interference

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:33.261
to any radio communications
of any station license

00:13:33.261 --> 00:13:35.910
or authorized by or under this chapter

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:37.360
operated by the United States government."

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:39.610
And since signal jammers and scramblers

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:41.833
are capable of interfering
with radio communications

00:13:41.833 --> 00:13:44.070
the feds have made them illegal.

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:46.410
Now jamming devices cannot
be certified or authorized

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:48.950
because their primary purpose
is to block or interfere

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:50.730
with authorized radio communications.

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:53.570
And therefore their use would
compromise the integrity

00:13:53.570 --> 00:13:55.850
of the nation's
communication infrastructure.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:58.012
And of course another
obviously illegal product

00:13:58.012 --> 00:13:59.900
is a license plate flipper.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.780
There's no doubt, they look cool.

00:14:01.780 --> 00:14:03.460
They make you feel just like James Bond.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.662
- Revolving number plates, naturally.

00:14:05.662 --> 00:14:07.300
Valid in all countries.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:09.320
- Now a license plate flipper
generally allows a driver

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:12.280
to temporarily flip and or
hide their license plate

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:15.740
in order to avoid detection
from traffic cameras

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:19.310
and toll booths and police
that are chasing you.

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:23.050
And they could also help you
hide from mobsters, spies,

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:25.360
jealous lovers, all depending
on what you're into.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:28.470
Now needless to say these
are completely, totally

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:30.180
and unequivocally illegal.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.780
Though admittedly, there is another

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:33.760
potentially less nefarious reason

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.480
for having a license plate cover.

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:36.490
Now we live a world

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:38.040
where there seems to be
surveillance everywhere,

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:41.010
both online and offline and
automated license plate readers

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:44.810
known as ALPRs scan license
plates of parked cars

00:14:44.810 --> 00:14:47.050
or cars that are in traffic.

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:49.830
When uploaded to a central
database they can track

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:51.890
all the places that a vehicle may turn up.

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:53.970
That means that everything
about your daily habits

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:56.110
could be tracked because this information

00:14:56.110 --> 00:14:57.700
is out in the public.

00:14:57.700 --> 00:14:59.690
Now, sometimes this valuable information

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:02.680
is even sold to third parties
like debt collectors, lenders,

00:15:02.680 --> 00:15:04.700
insurance companies,
and other shady groups.

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:07.340
Now California legislators
considered allowing people

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:10.030
to simply cover their
license plates when parked

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:12.280
and there was bipartisan
support for the measure

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:13.940
but lobbyists effectively killed the bill.

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:15.430
That means that businesses
still have the right

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:18.350
to mount ALPRs on vehicles
and drive them around the city

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.220
taking photographs of every license plate.

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:22.240
And that also means that
law enforcement agencies

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:24.850
have the ability to collect the
same data from your vehicle.

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:27.050
And in 2018, the Department
of Homeland security

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:29.300
updated its policies to give ICE,

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:31.740
the agency responsible for immigration,

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:34.240
access to license plate
recognition databases.

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:36.810
And civil libertarians are right
to be concerned about this.

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:38.670
As of two years ago, The
Atlantic reported that vigilant,

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:41.660
a company that amasses this information

00:15:41.660 --> 00:15:45.090
had collected roughly 2.2
billion license plate photos

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:46.560
and was capturing and permanently storing

00:15:46.560 --> 00:15:49.560
about 80 million additional
geo tag images per month.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:50.750
But let's talk about a product

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:53.510
that I was actually
surprised is very illegal.

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:56.830
'Cause I see this one a lot,
especially in the movies.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:59.008
Now fans of the insanely
popular movie franchise

00:15:59.008 --> 00:16:01.380
"The Fast and the Furious" have been eager

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:05.170
to buy nitrous oxide kits
to soup up their cars.

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:07.040
Racers use these kits to
give their cars a boost

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:09.070
in street races and on the track.

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.760
And generally speaking a nitrous oxide kit

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:13.510
is generally safe if it's
used for 15 seconds or less,

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:14.650
but does that mean it's legal for you

00:16:14.650 --> 00:16:16.710
to pretend to be Vin Diesel while driving?

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:18.770
Well, you can legally shave your head

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:21.650
but you cannot use a nitrous oxide kit

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:22.547
while publicly driving.

00:16:22.547 --> 00:16:24.960
Race car drivers have the
legal right to use nitrous

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.896
on the track and so do
private property owners

00:16:26.896 --> 00:16:28.930
when you're driving on private property.

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:30.850
And nitrous oxide is not
a controlled substance.

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:32.831
You can buy, sell or transport it.

00:16:32.831 --> 00:16:35.150
But when it comes to street vehicles,

00:16:35.150 --> 00:16:36.740
it depends on the state and local laws.

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:38.210
California has some of the strictest laws

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:40.250
on vehicle modifications
and aftermarket parts.

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:43.139
And it is absolutely illegal
to have a nitrous system

00:16:43.139 --> 00:16:45.490
without a carb certification installed

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:47.300
on your street vehicle in California.

00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:49.940
Some local counties and
municipalities do emissions testing

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:52.560
and a nitrous system would
absolutely wreck havoc

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:54.050
on that particular test.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:55.190
And Ohio is another state

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:56.780
that strictly regulates nitrous oxide.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:58.974
It's not legal to use
nitrous in a car in Ohio.

00:16:58.974 --> 00:17:01.650
So if you buy a nitrous oxide there,

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:03.030
you are required to sign a form

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:05.710
declaring that you know it's
illegal to use in the car.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:07.298
But let's face it if you
install nitrous oxide

00:17:07.298 --> 00:17:11.100
on your 93 Honda civic
you're probably gonna end up

00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:12.700
like Hoovies Garage anyway.

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:13.713
- And button.

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:15.743
Whoa.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:21.890
Oh Jesus, I just blew the motor.

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:23.793
I just completely blew the motor.

00:17:23.793 --> 00:17:26.770
- Then getting back to some
real "James Bond" stuff.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:28.730
I know that when you're
dealing with terrible traffic

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:31.400
and horrible drivers
that the urge to deploy

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.910
some spikes and just blow up the tires

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:35.330
of everyone else that's on the road.

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:37.720
It's a very strong urge.

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:40.150
I regret to inform you that is illegal.

00:17:40.150 --> 00:17:42.620
Now a caltrop is a weapon
that has been around

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:44.920
for some form for thousands of years.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:46.960
It's a passive weapon that projects spikes

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:47.820
in different directions,

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:50.770
preventing horses, camels,
elephants and land vehicles

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:51.680
from moving forward.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:52.910
The Ukrainian military

00:17:52.910 --> 00:17:54.630
has been making good use of them lately.

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.860
And Doomsday Preppers
are eager to buy these

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:58.632
as they wait for the zombie deep state

00:17:58.632 --> 00:18:00.310
queued on COVID apocalypse.

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:03.910
And even some car monitors have
created secret compartments

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:08.170
that hide caltrops to be
deployed against your enemies

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:09.090
that are following you.

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:11.230
These kinds of devices
are completely illegal

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:14.410
under a whole myriad of
different general purpose laws.

00:18:14.410 --> 00:18:16.410
But many states have specific regulations

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:19.170
that make caltrops and
tire spikes illegal to use

00:18:19.170 --> 00:18:20.930
unless they're used by law enforcement

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:23.040
for incredibly obvious reasons.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:25.620
And Texas, for example,
specifically banned caltrops

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:27.460
after drug dealers started using them.

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:29.820
And in Texas a person can
be charged with a felony

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:31.310
if they intentionally or knowingly

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:34.090
possess manufactured
transport, repair or sell

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:37.330
a tire deflation device such as a caltrop.

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:41.480
So unless you are law enforcement
do not use tire spikes

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:42.609
of any kind.

00:18:42.609 --> 00:18:45.340
Speaking of which, if
you're not law enforcement

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:47.760
don't pretend to be law enforcement.

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:51.330
And for that reason it is
illegal to use car strobe lights

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:52.780
that flash red and blue

00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:55.330
because it makes you look
like a police officer.

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:58.750
Nonetheless, you can buy some
of these products on Amazon.

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:01.250
There's also all kinds
of illegal light products

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:02.083
on Amazon as well.

00:19:02.083 --> 00:19:05.670
And for the most part, buying
a light that can be mounted

00:19:05.670 --> 00:19:08.128
to a car truck isn't illegal for purchase

00:19:08.128 --> 00:19:09.680
but all states have different rules

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:12.450
about which vehicles can
use which kind of lights.

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:13.760
For example, in almost every state

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:16.060
only the police are allowed
to use blue and red lights

00:19:16.060 --> 00:19:16.930
on top of a car.

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:19.400
In many states only emergency
vehicles can use red lights

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:20.340
on top of the car.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:23.330
And some states restrict
the kind of flash patterns.

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:24.750
And then of course there are tons

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:26.260
of brightness restrictions as well.

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:29.020
Most of this means that states
don't allow auxiliary lights

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:30.790
that can be brighter
than a car's headlights

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:31.623
or brake lights

00:19:31.623 --> 00:19:33.960
because you don't want to be
installing aftermarket lights

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:35.840
that blind the people in front of you.

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:39.010
So I'm sorry to burst all
of your "James Bond" dreams,

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:40.460
but all of these products are illegal

00:19:40.460 --> 00:19:41.650
in some way or another.

00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:43.800
So if you do install any of these products

